  "prompt": "/deep-research Which U.S. states had a percentage of alcohol-impaired-driving traffic fatalities higher than 35% in 2022 according to the NHTSA’s Traffic Safety Facts report, and also had an excessive drinking rate above 20% in 2022 based on data from WorldPopulationReview.com?",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Which U.S. states had a percentage of alcohol-impaired-driving traffic fatalities higher than 35% in 2022 according to the NHTSA’s Traffic Safety Facts report, and also had an excessive drinking rate above 20% in 2022 based on data from WorldPopulationReview.com?",
  "answer": "## Answer\n\n**No states can be confirmed to meet both criteria** because the **WorldPopulationReview.com source for \"excessive drinking rate by state\" does not exist**.\n\n### NHTSA Data (Verified)\nFrom the NHTSA Traffic Safety Facts 2022 report (DOT HS 813 578), Table 4, these states had **>35% alcohol-impaired-driving fatalities**:\n\n| State | % Alcohol-Impaired Fatalities |\n|-------|------------------------------|\n| Rhode Island | 43% |\n| South Carolina | 43% |\n| Texas | 42% |\n| District of Columbia | 39% |\n| Oregon | 39% |\n| Illinois | 37% |\n| Maryland | 37% |\n| Ohio | 37% |\n| New Hampshire | 36% |\n\n**Source:** [https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/813578](https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/813578)\n\n### WorldPopulationReview Data (Not Found)\nExtensive searching confirmed:\n- `worldpopulationreview.com/state-rankings/excessive-drinking-rate-by-state` → **404 Not Found**\n- All variants (`excessive-drinking-by-state`, `excessive-drinking-rates-by-state`, `excessive-drinking-rate-by-state-2022`, etc.) → **404**\n- **Zero snapshots** in the Wayback Machine for any of these URLs\n- The site's only alcohol-related state ranking is **\"Alcohol Consumption by State\"** — which reports **per-capita ethanol consumption in gallons**, not the percentage of adults engaging in excessive/binge drinking\n\n**Source checked:** [https://worldpopulationreview.com/state-rankings/alcohol-consumption-by-state](https://worldpopulationreview.com/state-rankings/alcohol-consumption-by-state)\n\n---\n\n### What You Can Do\nIf you need excessive drinking rates (% of adults binge/heavy drinking) by state for 2022, the authoritative source is **CDC BRFSS data as published by America's Health Rankings**:  \n`https://www.americashealthrankings.org/explore/measures/ExcessDrink`\n\nWould you like me to pull that data instead and cross-reference with the NHTSA list above?",
  "answer_chars": 1901,
  "expected_answer": "New Hampshire, South Carolina, Ohio, Illinois, Oregon, Rhode Island",
